WEBVTT

00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:15.000
Active recall is the practice of retrieving information from memory rather than simply rereading it. Close your notes, explain the idea, then compare your explanation with the source.

00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:30.000
Spaced repetition means revisiting information over increasing intervals. The right interval depends on how easily you recall the material.

00:00:31.000 --> 00:00:45.000
Feedback helps compare performance with a desired result. First, recall the idea. Next, check missing qualifications. Finally, write a question to revisit tomorrow.
